@page "/cli"
<PageTitle>CLI - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">CLI</h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">The Blaizio CLI (<code>blaizio</code>) exists because the styled layer is <em>your source, not a package</em>. It copies components from a registry into your project, rewrites them to your namespace, resolves their dependencies (both registry items and NuGet packages), records what's installed, and wires the Tailwind toolchain - so a component you add today is a file you can open, read and edit tomorrow. Install: <code>dotnet tool install -g Blaizio.Cli</code>. Update the tool itself with <code>dotnet tool update -g Blaizio.Cli</code>.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Global options</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Every command accepts these. <code>--yes</code>, <code>--json</code> or <code>--silent</code> makes a run non-interactive (no prompts, defaults win). With <code>--json</code>, results go to stdout as machine-readable JSON and errors to stderr - built for scripts, IDE plugins and MCP.</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Option</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-c, --cwd &lt;DIR&gt;</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Working directory (defaults to the current directory).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-y, --yes</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Skip prompts, accept defaults.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-s, --silent</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Mute output.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--json</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Emit JSON.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--registry &lt;URL&gt;</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Registry base URL or local path - overrides <code>blaizio.json</code>.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Exit codes: <code>0</code> success · <code>1</code> error (also: <code>diff</code> found drift) · <code>2</code> registry error · <code>130</code> cancelled (Ctrl+C). Set <code>BLAIZIO_DEBUG=1</code> for full stack traces.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">blaizio init</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">The default command - running bare <code>blaizio</code> starts it interactively. It initializes a project: writes <code>blaizio.json</code>, installs the base NuGet packages (<code>Blaizio.Base</code>, <code>Blaizio.Icons</code>, <code>TailwindMerge.NET</code>), writes the theme CSS (<code>Styles/blaizio/*</code> + <code>Styles/app.css</code>), wires a Tailwind pipeline, patches your <b>host page</b> - whichever the app has: <code>wwwroot/index.html</code> (WASM), <code>Components/App.razor</code> (Blazor Web App) or <code>Pages/_Host.cshtml</code> / <code>_Layout.cshtml</code> (Blazor Server) - inserting the <code>style-*</code> skin class (plus <code>dir="rtl"</code> when RTL), the compiled stylesheet link and the pre-paint <code>boot.js</code> script into the existing file, optionally scaffolds a whole app from a template, and adds any components you pass as arguments. Re-running <code>init</code> on an initialized project is a <b>top-up</b>: it keeps the recorded config (explicit flags still override) and adds only whatever is missing; <code>--force</code> starts over instead.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Cli/Init" />
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Option</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Default</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>[COMPONENTS]</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">-</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Components to add right after initializing.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-t, --template</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">prompted</td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>showcase</code> · <code>webapp</code> · <code>wasm</code> · <code>library</code> (see Templates below).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-n, --name</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">assembly name</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Project name for a scaffolded template.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--namespace</code> <span class="text-muted-foreground">(-ns)</span></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>{Root}.Components.Ui</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Root namespace every copied component is rewritten to.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-o, --output</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>Components/Ui</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Directory copied components are written to.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--theme</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>ember</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Skin: <code>ash</code>, <code>aura</code>, <code>ember</code>, <code>flint</code>, <code>forge</code>, <code>glow</code>, <code>spark</code>, <code>wisp</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--tailwind</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>auto</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Pipeline: <code>auto</code>, <code>standalone</code>, <code>node</code>, <code>vite</code>, <code>rollup</code>, <code>postcss</code>, <code>none</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--rtl</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">off</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Enable RTL support.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--pointer</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">off</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Pointer cursor on buttons (an extra managed CSS file).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-d, --defaults</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">off</td><td class="px-3 py-2">No prompts, all defaults (implies template <code>showcase</code>).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-f, --force</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">off</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Overwrite an existing <code>blaizio.json</code> / scaffold files.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="pt-2 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Templates</h3>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Template</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">What you get</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>showcase</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">A complete WebAssembly demo app: layout with sidebar, command palette and theme toggle; dashboard, forms, overlays, data and auth pages; ~35 components pre-added. The best way to see everything working.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>library</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">A Razor class library wired for Blaizio (Razor SDK, framework reference, packages, imports) - for building a shared component library. An existing bare class library is hardened in place.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>webapp</code> / <code>wasm</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Config, packages and styling are wired; the page scaffolding for these templates is still in progress - use <code>dotnet new</code> first and run <code>blaizio init</code> inside.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">blaizio add</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Copies components into your project. For each item the CLI resolves its <em>registry dependencies</em> transitively (dependency-first order, each item once), installs the aggregated <em>NuGet dependencies</em>, writes the files under your output directory, rewrites every namespace to yours, tops up <code>_Imports.razor</code> (plus a project-wide global using for the base namespace), and records the item in <code>blaizio.json</code>. Existing files are <b>skipped</b> unless you pass <code>--overwrite</code> - your edits are safe by default. With no arguments it opens an interactive picker.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Cli/Add" />
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Option</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>[COMPONENTS]</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Names, URLs, or local <code>.json</code> paths. Empty → interactive picker.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-a, --all</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Add every component in the registry.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--overwrite</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Overwrite existing files (default: skip them).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--prune</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Delete files in the output directory no registry item ships anymore (requires <code>--all</code>).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--dry-run</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Resolve and report only - nothing written, nothing installed.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--no-deps</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Skip NuGet installs <em>and</em> transitive registry dependencies.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--no-nuget</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Skip only the NuGet install (monorepo / ProjectReference setups).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>-o, --output</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Destination override for this run.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>--namespace</code> <span class="text-muted-foreground">(-ns)</span></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Namespace override for this run.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Browse, inspect &amp; keep in sync</h2>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Cli/Maintain" />
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Command</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>list</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">List registry components. <code>-q</code> filters by name/title/description, <code>-l</code> (default 100) and <code>--offset</code> page.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>search &lt;QUERY&gt;</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Shorthand for <code>list -q</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>view &lt;ITEMS&gt;</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Print a component's metadata, dependencies and full file contents - without writing anything.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>diff [COMPONENT]</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Compare installed files against the registry (all installed when no argument). Exits <code>1</code> on any drift - CI-friendly, like <code>git diff --exit-code</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>update [COMPONENTS]</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Re-pull components (default: everything installed), overwriting local copies - then re-ensure the CSS assets and host-page wiring, so it also repairs a partially-wired project.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>upgrade</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Bump the Blaizio NuGet packages to this tool's pinned versions, then re-pull every installed component. <code>update</code> = source only; <code>upgrade</code> = versions + source.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>info</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Show the resolved project + configuration (tool version, csproj, namespace, output, theme, registry, ...).</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">blaizio tailwind</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Blaizio needs Tailwind v4 to compile <code>Styles/app.css</code> into <code>wwwroot/app.css</code>. The <code>tailwind</code> commands inspect and wire that pipeline. <code>auto</code> prefers an existing setup (<code>vite</code> &gt; <code>rollup</code> &gt; <code>postcss</code> &gt; <code>node</code> &gt; <code>standalone</code>) and never clobbers a bundler you already have; on a bare project it picks <code>standalone</code>.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Cli/Tailwind" />
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Pipeline</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">How it compiles</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>standalone</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><b>Zero Node.</b> Setup writes <code>.blaizio/Blaizio.Tailwind.targets</code> and imports it into your csproj - the native <code>tailwindcss</code> binary runs on every <code>dotnet build</code> / <code>dotnet watch</code>. The binary auto-downloads into a per-user cache on first build (or pre-fetch it, sha256-verified, with <code>tailwind fetch</code>). MSBuild knobs: <code>BlaizioTailwindVersion</code>, <code>BlaizioTailwindAutoFetch</code>, <code>BlaizioTailwindInput/Output/Exe</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>node</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Adds <code>@@tailwindcss/cli</code> as a devDependency plus <code>css</code> / <code>css:watch</code> scripts to <code>package.json</code> (package manager detected from your lockfile: pnpm / yarn / bun / npm). You run the install yourself.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>vite</code> / <code>rollup</code> / <code>postcss</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Detected and respected when already present - the CLI reports them but doesn't set them up. Vite uses <code>@@tailwindcss/vite</code>; Rollup and PostCSS-based bundlers (webpack etc.) host <code>@@tailwindcss/postcss</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>none</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Writes only the input CSS; compiling is yours to arrange.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm"><code>tailwind fetch</code> options: <code>--tw-version</code> (a release tag or <code>latest</code>; default <code>v4.1.11</code>), <code>--musl</code> (Alpine builds; auto-detected), <code>-f, --force</code> (re-download). The cache lives under <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\blaizio\cache</code> (Windows), <code>~/Library/Caches/blaizio</code> (macOS) or <code>~/.cache/blaizio</code> (Linux) - override with the <code>BLAIZIO_CACHE_DIR</code> environment variable; one download serves every project.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">blaizio.json</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">The per-project configuration, written by <code>init</code> and kept current by <code>add</code>. Commit it - the <code>installed</code> map is what powers <code>diff</code> and no-argument <code>update</code>.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="Cli/Config" />
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
            <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr class="border-b bg-muted/50"><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Key</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Default</th><th class="px-3 py-2 text-start font-medium">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-muted-foreground [&_code]:text-foreground">
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>namespace</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">required</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Root namespace applied to every copied component.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>output</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>Components/Ui</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Where copied components land (project-relative).</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>theme</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>ember</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">The active skin's token set.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>rtl</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>false</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Whether RTL was wired at init.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>registry</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>https://blaiz.io/r</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Registry base URL, or a local path (resolved against the project). <code>--registry</code> overrides per run.</td></tr>
                    <tr class="border-b"><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>aliases</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>base: Blaizio</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Namespace aliases - <code>base</code> is the headless layer's namespace (drives the generated usings), <code>ui</code> mirrors <code>namespace</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap"><code>installed</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2"><code>{}</code></td><td class="px-3 py-2">Every added item and the files it wrote - maintained by the CLI.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The registry &amp; maintainer commands</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">A registry is a folder of JSON served over HTTP (or sitting on disk): an <code>index.json</code> catalogue plus one <code>&lt;name&gt;.json</code> per item with its file contents inlined. <code>add</code> accepts bare names (resolved against the registry base), full URLs, or local paths - so private and third-party registries work with nothing more than <code>--registry</code> or a URL. Two commands exist for people <em>publishing</em> a registry: <code>generate [SOURCE]</code> scans a component source tree into a <code>registry.json</code> manifest (inferring cross-component dependencies), and <code>build [MANIFEST] -o &lt;DIR&gt;</code> compiles that manifest into the servable per-item JSON + index. This docs site serves its own build at <code>/r</code>.</p>
    </section>
</div>
